Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayGraphics3D", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"7f2368a2-e024-5a47-95e9-b4774ef0b3e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7ef9f64b-dae8-914e-8051-f08406346e9e"],
 " ",
 "draws the array arr as cubes arranged in space."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"f710bc6e-27a5-0d41-a8f1-5d0ddeba87ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr", ",", " ", "opts"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"174e5368-40eb-e448-b54a-ab66783404dc"],
 " ",
 "draws it with the given options."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"8a73c921-af64-9e43-b928-539411c91a4d"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"7518c029-0cac-3f4a-9358-8d2fa958a564"],

Cell["\<\
An array of order one is drawn as a line of cubes, one of order two as a \
plane of them, and one of order three as a lattice. The entry at index tuple \
(i, j, k) sits at the point {i, j, k}, an index the array does not have \
standing at one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"058d9a92-2805-ca40-b388-328f43091caf"],

Cell["\<\
An array of higher order is drawn by tiling: the inner block of indices is \
drawn as a lattice, and the outer block repeats that lattice through space, \
shifted by its own extent and a gap. Everything ends up in one picture, since \
space has no room for pictures inset into pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6b393c42-fb03-cc48-8f20-e4015ea6ebb9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is always a three-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Graphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0441f537-a96c-a448-97bb-24a3604e1fed"],
 ". For plane pictures at every order see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f4307e3-faac-fd49-882e-2d8ae08f2975"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9350db4d-4587-4643-b1e1-0c356c63824a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Nesting\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k1", ",", " ", "k2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f02bb790-70e3-0043-a695-568e28bf12a5"],
 " says how to split the indices: the blocks must sum to the order of the \
array and each must be one, two or three, space holding no more at a time. \
The default uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayNesting", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"04dc0535-1720-2546-9b87-e0e80f4e984d"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3479e398-d1b8-294a-8a57-47ab07ec747a"],

Cell["\<\
The cubes have translucent faces and no outline, so that the entries behind \
them can still be read; an outline on every cube of a lattice reads as a mesh \
rather than as a set of cells.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b77b09c7-8f3d-1143-8d58-36a9216d6e16"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A gnomon in the near corner marks as many axes as the picture uses; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Gnomon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"954d04b7-bf51-5641-a156-c8b423518914"],
 " drops it. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Indices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Colored\>\""}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "52687241-1673-fb46-8f5a-8cea65c86bd9"],
 " gives each axis a colour of its own."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5796985c-9309-614f-9aba-586ccbba398f"],

Cell["\<\
The reference implementation this package grew out of drew only the \
order-three case, and called such a picture a cubix; the name is not kept, \
but the look of it is.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5d597bee-de1d-8f4e-b642-0e649e173d82"],

Cell["The other options are shared with ArrayGraphics.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a00a0538-1b1d-3447-9a72-63a66839db53"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"095a51d9-e882-9841-acda-2c1ee7b6c7c2"],

Cell["At order one a line of cubes, at order two a plane of them:", \
"ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"118bb571-6079-694d-bc55-f790858bee04"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics3D[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics3D[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"62acfa14-0683-e84a-b522-0917249096b1"],

